---
import UntranslatedLayout from '~/layouts/UntranslatedLayout.astro';
---

<UntranslatedLayout title="Privacy Policy - BeHonor Studio" description="Privacy Policy for BeHonor Studio Apps.">
    <div class="pt-32 pb-24">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-foreground/80">
                <p class="text-lg mb-6">Last updated: September 4, 2026</p>

                <p>
                    This Privacy Policy describes Our policies and procedures on the collection, use and disclosure of Your information when You use our applications and services, and tells You about Your privacy rights and how the law protects You.
                </p>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4 text-foreground">Interpretation and Definitions</h2>
                
                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-foreground">Interpretation</h3>
                <p>
                    The words of which the initial letter is capitalized have meanings defined under the following conditions. The following definitions shall have the same meaning regardless of whether they appear in singular or in plural.
                </p>

                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-foreground">Definitions</h3>
                <p>For the purposes of this Privacy Policy:</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
                    <li><strong>Account</strong> means a unique account created for You to access our Service or parts of our Service.</li>
                    <li><strong>Affiliate</strong> means an entity that controls, is controlled by or is under common control with a party, where "control" means ownership of 50% or more of the shares, equity interest or other securities entitled to vote for election of directors or other managing authority.</li>
                    <li><strong>Application</strong> refers to the software programs provided by the Company, including "ISS Tracker", "Check My Device", and other applications published by BeHonor Studio.</li>
                    <li><strong>Company</strong> (referred to as either "the Company", "We", "Us" or "Our" in this Agreement) refers to BeHonor Studio.</li>
                    <li><strong>Device</strong> means any device that can access the Service such as a computer, a cellphone or a digital tablet.</li>
                    <li><strong>Personal Data</strong> is any information that relates to an identified or identifiable individual.</li>
                    <li><strong>Service</strong> refers to the Applications provided by the Company.</li>
                    <li><strong>Service Provider</strong> means any natural or legal person who processes the data on behalf of the Company, such as third-party advertising networks.</li>
                    <li><strong>Usage Data</strong> refers to data collected automatically, either generated by the use of the Service or from the Service infrastructure itself.</li>
                    <li><strong>You</strong> means the individual accessing or using the Service, or the company, or other legal entity on behalf of which such individual is accessing or using the Service, as applicable.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4 text-foreground">Information Collection and Use</h2>

                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-foreground">1. Personal Data</h3>
                <p>
                    We do not collect, transmit, or store any personal identification information (such as your name, email address, physical address, or phone number). Our applications do not require user account registration or login.
                </p>

                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-foreground">2. Location Data (On-Device Processing Only)</h3>
                <p>
                    Certain features in our applications (such as the pass prediction feature in <strong>ISS Tracker</strong>) require access to your device's location (approximate or precise) to calculate and display the satellite's next visible pass over your current position.
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
                    <li>Location data is processed strictly in-memory on your device (ephemeral processing).</li>
                    <li>We <strong>never</strong> upload, transmit, or store your location on any remote server.</li>
                    <li>We <strong>never</strong> share or sell your location data to any third party or advertiser.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-foreground">3. Third-Party Advertising (Google AdMob)</h3>
                <p>
                    To support our free services, our applications may display advertisements powered by <strong>Google AdMob</strong>. The Google Mobile Ads SDK may automatically collect and process certain device information to serve ads, prevent fraud, and analyze ad performance. This may include:
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
                    <li><strong>Device or other IDs:</strong> such as the Google Advertising ID (GAID) or other device identifiers.</li>
                    <li><strong>App Activity & Interactions:</strong> user interactions with advertisements (views, impressions, and clicks).</li>
                    <li><strong>App Performance & Diagnostics:</strong> diagnostic and error logs, ad loading latency, and performance data.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="mt-4">
                    All data transmitted by the AdMob SDK is encrypted in transit using industry-standard HTTPS protocols. For more information about how Google collects and processes user data, please review:
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mt-4">
                    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
                    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a></li>
                </ul>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4 text-foreground">Children's Privacy and Families Policy</h2>
                <p>
                    We are committed to protecting children's privacy and complying with the <strong>Google Play Families Policy</strong> and the Children's Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under the age of 13.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4">
                    For applications whose target audience includes children, all third-party advertisements are restricted to family-safe categories, and ads are requested in compliance with applicable child-directed regulations (such as using non-personalized ads).
                </p>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4 text-foreground">Links to Other Websites</h2>
                <p>
                    Our Service may contain links to other websites that are not operated by Us. If You click on a third party link, You will be directed to that third party's site. We strongly advise You to review the Privacy Policy of every site You visit.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4">
                    We have no control over and assume no responsibility for the content, privacy policies or practices of any third party sites or services.
                </p>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4 text-foreground">Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
                <p>
                    We may update Our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify You of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4">
                    We will let You know via email and/or a prominent notice on Our Service, prior to the change becoming effective and update the "Last updated" date at the top of this Privacy Policy.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-4">
                    You are advised to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes. Changes to this Privacy Policy are effective when they are posted on this page.
                </p>

                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-4 text-foreground">Contact Us</h2>
                <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at: <a href="mailto:beehonorstu@gmail.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">beehonorstu@gmail.com</a></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</UntranslatedLayout>
